# Social app post search

## Overview

Post search is **server-backed**, not a client-side filter over the home feed. The UI debounces input (300 ms) and calls [`searchPosts`](apps/social/src/services/search.service.ts), which queries Strapi **`GET /posts`** with `$containsi` filters.

## Service contract

| Export | Role |
|--------|------|
| `searchPosts(query, options?)` | Returns `HomeFeedPost[]` via `normalizeStrapiPostEntry` |
| `SearchPostsOptions` | `limit`, `page`, `signal` |
| `SEARCH_SUGGESTION_LIMIT` | `6` — header [`SearchBar`](apps/social/src/components/SearchBar.tsx) |
| `SEARCH_RESULTS_PAGE_SIZE` | `48` — [`/search`](apps/social/src/app/search/page.tsx) |

### Strapi query (built in `buildSearchQuery`)

- **Filters:** `filters[$or][0][Title][$containsi]` and `filters[$or][1][Slug][$containsi]` (trimmed query string).
- **Populate:** same card shape as feed — `CoverImage`, `Media` (url, mime, alternativeText), `post_likes` / `post_comments` counts.
- **Sort:** `createdAt:desc`
- **Cache:** `apiClient.get(..., { cache: "no-store" })` so typing always hits the API.

### Do not

- Call `getHomeFeedPosts()` and `.filter()` in the browser for search.
- Use `next: { revalidate }` on search requests (feed-only).

## UI integration

- **Header:** [`SearchBar.tsx`](apps/social/src/components/SearchBar.tsx) — min 2 chars, `AbortController` per debounced request, `limit: SEARCH_SUGGESTION_LIMIT`.
- **Page:** [`search/page.tsx`](apps/social/src/app/search/page.tsx) — reads `?q=`, debounced via [`SearchInput`](apps/social/src/components/search/SearchInput.tsx), `limit: SEARCH_RESULTS_PAGE_SIZE`, abort on query change.
- **Results:** [`SearchResultsGrid`](apps/social/src/components/search/SearchResultsGrid.tsx) → `HomePostsCollage` with `likeMode="api"`.

On abort or unmount, do not toast; check `abortController.signal.aborted` in `catch`.

## Backend / permissions

- Posts: public `find` on `api::post.post` ([`apps/backend/src/index.ts`](apps/backend/src/index.ts) role grants).
- No dedicated `post.search` route yet; Strapi REST filters are sufficient for title/slug search.
- **User/profile search** is out of scope — no public user-discovery API is wired in social [`api-endpoints.ts`](apps/social/src/lib/api-endpoints.ts).

## When to add a custom `post.search` endpoint

Consider a backend custom route (mirror `product.search`) if you need:

- Full-text / `Description` (richtext) search with sanitization
- Ranked or fuzzy matching
- Combined post + story + user results
- Stricter rate limits or search analytics

Until then, extend `search.service.ts` filters only.

